{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789241985,"nonce":"H7ZEsbd1eld+uvVq7Z0gfQN6Kxs=","title":"zb_str_cmp read the string plugin's i32 compare result as i64","message":"`$String$compare` returns i32 in {-1, 0, 1}. The library declared it as\ni64, so the upper half of the register was whatever the callee left\nthere and `-1` read as 4294967295: `\"a\" \u003c \"b\"` was false through\n`zb_str_lt`, and every sort of strings in a dynamic list came out\nreversed while a typed `List\u003cstr\u003e` sort, which never reached the\ncompare, was right.\n\nFix: declare the primitive i32 and compare against an i32 zero. The\nother i32-returning primitives (equals, contains, starts_with,\nends_with) are declared bool and read the low byte, which is correct.","files":null}]}